  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Frameworks Options**\n\nI\'m currently evaluating the best framework options for the Rotaract Club landing page. The user initially wanted a single HTML file, but now I\'m considering Next.js or Nest.js. The primary constraint is that the code needs to be functional when opened directly. I\'m leaning toward Next.js but will also compare against Nest.js with the standalone output.\n\n\n**Deciding on Implementation**\n\nI\'ve determined that a single-page React application using Tailwind CSS is the best approach, given the Vite/React environment. I\'ll adhere to the Rotaract Club\'s branding and structure, utilizing IntersectionObserver for fade-ins, animated counters, and smooth scrolling for user interactions. The mobile hamburger menu will also be included. The layout is planned as a single page with sections for navigation, hero, impact numbers, about us, board of directors, past projects, events/news, partners/volunteers, donation, and the footer.\n\n\n"
