    user_requests: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^1.29.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.0\nreact-dom: ^19.0.0\nvite: ^6.2.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.0\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": []\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig, loadEnv} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(({mode}) => {\n  const env = loadEnv(mode, \'.\', \'\');\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    define: {\n      \'process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY\': JSON.stringify(env.GEMINI_API_KEY),\n    },\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    user_requests: "You are a senior frontend engineer and UI/UX designer specializing in nonprofit and \ncommunity organization websites. Your work is benchmarked against award-winning sites. \nlike the Obama Foundation (2025 Webby Award Winner), Giving Kitchen (WebAward Best \nNonprofit), and charity: water\342\200\224not generic template sites. It should all be done in Next.js\n\n---\n\n## PROJECT BRIEF\n\nBuild a complete, production-ready website for:\n\n**Organization:** Rotaract Club of Ring Road Ibadan\n**Type:** Community service and youth leadership club under Rotary International\n**Location:** Ibadan, Nigeria\n**Audience:** Young professionals (18\342\200\22330), potential donors, partner organizations, \nsponsors, and the general public\n**Goal:** Establish a strong digital presence that communicates mission, showcases \nimpact, drives donations, and attracts partnerships\n\n---\n\n## DELIVERABLE\n\nA single, self-contained HTML file with embedded CSS and JavaScript. \nNo external dependencies except Google Fonts and Font Awesome (CDN links allowed). \nNo frameworks. Pure HTML, CSS (with CSS variables), and vanilla JS.\n\nThe site must be:\n- Fully responsive (mobile-first)\n- Smooth scrolling with clean section transitions\n- Visually excellent \342\200\224 NOT a generic template. Every section must feel intentional.\n- Fast loading \342\200\224 no heavy animations, no bloat\n\n---\n\n## BRAND IDENTITY\n\n**Primary Color:** Royal Blue \342\200\224 #003F87 (Rotary International brand color)\n**Accent Color:** Gold \342\200\224 #F7A81B (Rotaract accent)\n**Background:** #FFFFFF with subtle off-white sections (#F8F9FA)\n**Text:** #1A1A2E for headings, #4A4A68 for body\n**Font:** Use \"Inter\" from Google Fonts for all text\n\nVisual rule: The site must feel premium and modern. Think clean whitespace, \nstrong typographic hierarchy, and purposeful use of the blue/gold brand palette. \nNot corporate, not stuffy \342\200\224 it should feel like a club run by sharp, driven young \npeople who take their service seriously.\n\n---\n\n## PAGES / SECTIONS (single-page layout with anchor navigation)\n\nBuild the following sections in this exact order:\n\n### 1. NAVIGATION (sticky)\n- Logo text: \"Rotaract Ring Road\" in bold (blue)\n- Nav links: Home | About | Board | Projects | Events | Partner | Donate\n- \"Donate\" is a gold CTA button, always visible\n- Mobile: hamburger menu with smooth slide-down drawer\n- On scroll: navbar gets a white background with subtle shadow\n\n### 2. HERO SECTION\n- Full-width, bold. NOT a stock image background. Use a solid deep blue (#003F87) \n  with a subtle geometric pattern overlay (CSS-generated dots or diagonal lines).\n- Left side: \n  - Small tag: \"Service Above Self \302\267 Ibadan, Nigeria\"\n  - Large headline (60px+): \"Young Leaders. Real Service. Lasting Impact.\"\n  - Subheading: \"Rotaract Club of Ring Road Ibadan empowers young professionals to \n    take action in their communities and lead meaningful change.\"\n  - Two CTAs: [Get Involved \342\206\222] (white, filled) and [Our Projects] (white, outlined)\n- Right side: A CSS-illustrated or SVG abstract composition \342\200\224 layered cards, \n  circles, lines \342\200\224 in blue and gold. Suggest something geometric that conveys \n  community and connection. Do not use placeholder images.\n- Scroll indicator at the bottom\n\n### 3. IMPACT NUMBERS (full-width strip, blue background, gold accents)\nFour stats displayed in a clean row:\n- 50+ Members\n- 12+ Projects Completed\n- 1000+ Lives Impacted\n- 5+ Years of Service\n\nLarge animated counter numbers (count up on scroll into view using IntersectionObserver).\nEach stat has a small gold icon above it.\n\n### 4. ABOUT US\nTwo-column layout:\n- Left: Section label + large heading + 2\342\200\2233 paragraphs about the club \342\200\224 its mission, \n  its connection to Rotary International, its focus on youth service, community \n  development, and leadership in Ibadan.\n- Right: A stack of three \"value cards\" in blue/gold \342\200\224 \"Community\", \"Leadership\", \n  \"Service\" \342\200\224 each with a short one-liner and an icon.\n- Below: A blue strip with the Rotary motto \"Service Above Self\" in large italic gold text.\n\n### 5. BOARD OF DIRECTORS\nSection title: \"Meet the Board\"\nSubtitle: \"The 2025\342\200\2232026 leadership team driving our mission forward.\"\n\nDisplay board members as professional cards in a 3-column grid (2 on tablet, 1 on mobile):\nEach card has:\n- A circular avatar placeholder (styled with initials in blue/gold)\n- Name (bold)\n- Role/Title\n- Short one-liner bio\n\nPre-populate with these actual board members (use real titles, invent professional \none-liner bios appropriate for each role):\n- President: [President Name \342\200\224 to be filled in]\n- Vice President & Secretary: Rtr. King Praise\n- Welfare Director: [Name \342\200\224 to be filled in]\n- (Add 3 more placeholder board members for completeness)\n\nStyle the President card slightly larger or with a gold border to denote leadership.\n\n### 6. PAST PROJECTS\nSection title: \"Our Impact in Action\"\nSubtitle: \"A snapshot of the work we\'ve done in Ibadan and beyond.\"\n\nDisplay 6 project cards in a 3-column grid (CSS Grid):\nEach card:\n- Icon (relevant Font Awesome icon, gold)\n- Project name (bold, blue)\n- Short description (2 lines)\n- A \"View More\" link (no destination needed)\n- Subtle hover state: card lifts with shadow, gold top border appears\n\nProject categories to cover (invent appropriate names):\n- Health & Wellness\n- Education Outreach\n- Environmental Action\n- Youth Empowerment\n- Community Development\n- Vocational Support\n\n### 7. EVENTS / NEWS\nSection title: \"What\'s Coming\"\nDisplay the next 3 upcoming events as horizontal cards:\n- Date badge (blue, bold)\n- Event name\n- Short description\n- Lead name\n- [Add to Calendar] button (placeholder)\n\nPre-populate with the actual confirmed events:\n1. May 10, 2026 \342\200\224 Club Meeting (Lead: Rtr. King Praise)\n2. May 24, 2026 \342\200\224 Joint Fellowship (Lead: Rtr. Risqat)\n3. June 13, 2026 \342\200\224 Rotary Fellowship Meeting (Lead: Rtr. Toffy)\n\n### 8. PARTNER WITH US\nTwo-column card layout:\nLeft card (blue background):\n- Title: \"Become a Partner\"\n- Text: For organizations looking to collaborate on community impact projects, \n  sponsor events, or align their brand with youth leadership in Ibadan.\n- CTA: [Partner With Us]\n\nRight card (gold/light background):\n- Title: \"Volunteer With Us\"\n- Text: Join our community of action. Whether you\'re a Rotaractor or not, \n  there\'s a place for you in our work.\n- CTA: [Get Involved]\n\n### 9. DONATE\nFull-width section, dark blue background, centered:\n- Headline: \"Your Support Drives Real Change\"\n- Subtext: \"Every contribution funds a project, equips a young leader, \n  or serves a community in need.\"\n- Three giving tiers displayed as cards:\n  - \342\202\2465,000 \342\200\224 \"Community Friend\"\n  - \342\202\24620,000 \342\200\224 \"Impact Partner\"\n  - \342\202\24650,000 \342\200\224 \"Champion of Service\"\n  Each card has a short note on what the amount achieves.\n- Large gold CTA button: [Donate Now]\n- Note below: \"Secure giving. Every naira is accounted for.\"\n\n### 10. FOOTER\nThree columns:\n- Column 1: Club name + tagline + social icons (Instagram, LinkedIn, X/Twitter, WhatsApp)\n- Column 2: Quick links (mirror the nav)\n- Column 3: Contact info \342\200\224 Ibadan, Nigeria | Email placeholder | Phone placeholder\nBottom strip: \"\302\251 2026 Rotaract Club of Ring Road Ibadan. District 9125 | Affiliated \nwith Rotary International\"\n\n---\n\n## INTERACTION & ANIMATION RULES\n\n- All sections fade-in on scroll using IntersectionObserver (subtle, not distracting)\n- Impact counter animates upward on scroll\n- Project cards have hover lift effect\n- Nav link has active underline tracking current section\n- Smooth scroll to section on nav link click\n- Mobile hamburger menu toggles cleanly\n- No carousels. No auto-playing anything.\n\n---\n\n## WHAT TO AVOID\n\n- No stock photo placeholders with broken images \342\200\224 use CSS/SVG visuals instead\n- No Lorem Ipsum \342\200\224 write real, appropriate placeholder text for a Nigerian Rotaract club\n- No generic bootstrap-looking layout\n- No more than 3 font weights\n- No gradient overload \342\200\224 use solid brand colors deliberately\n- Do not use inline event handlers \342\200\224 use addEventListener throughout\n\n---\n\n## OUTPUT FORMAT\n\nReturn the complete HTML file only. No explanation before or after. \nStart with <!DOCTYPE html> and end with </html>. \nThe code must work by opening the file directly in a browser with zero setup."
    user_requests: "You are a senior frontend engineer and UI/UX designer specializing in nonprofit and\ncommunity organization websites. Your work is benchmarked against award-winning sites.\nlike the Obama Foundation (2025 Webby Award Winner), Giving Kitchen (WebAward Best\nNonprofit), and charity: water\342\200\224not generic template sites. It should all be done in Next.js\nPROJECT BRIEF\nBuild a complete, production-ready website for:\nOrganization: Rotaract Club of Ring Road Ibadan\nType: Community service and youth leadership club under Rotary International\nLocation: Ibadan, Nigeria\nAudience: Young professionals (18\342\200\22330), potential donors, partner organizations,\nsponsors, and the general public\nGoal: Establish a strong digital presence that communicates mission, showcases\nimpact, drives donations, and attracts partnerships\nDELIVERABLE\nA single, self-contained HTML file with embedded CSS and JavaScript.\nNo external dependencies except Google Fonts and Font Awesome (CDN links allowed).\nNo frameworks. Pure HTML, CSS (with CSS variables), and vanilla JS.\nThe site must be:\nFully responsive (mobile-first)\nSmooth scrolling with clean section transitions\nVisually excellent \342\200\224 NOT a generic template. Every section must feel intentional.\nFast loading \342\200\224 no heavy animations, no bloat\nBRAND IDENTITY\nPrimary Color: Royal Blue \342\200\224 #003F87 (Rotary International brand color)\nAccent Color: Gold \342\200\224 #F7A81B (Rotaract accent)\nBackground: #FFFFFF with subtle off-white sections (#F8F9FA)\nText: #1A1A2E for headings, #4A4A68 for body\nFont: Use \"Inter\" from Google Fonts for all text\nVisual rule: The site must feel premium and modern. Think clean whitespace,\nstrong typographic hierarchy, and purposeful use of the blue/gold brand palette.\nNot corporate, not stuffy \342\200\224 it should feel like a club run by sharp, driven young\npeople who take their service seriously.\nPAGES / SECTIONS (single-page layout with