ing it with a better version. I have also added more sophisticated rotation animation to the gear and orbital rings, to create a convincing 3D rotary visual. I am now working on making the gear have an animated rotation on the Z-axis, with a bit of a wobble on the Y-axis.\n\n\n**Refining SVG Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating a refined SVG, a high-fidelity rotary wheel. I\'m focusing on ensuring it looks great. My attention is on the new, more sophisticated SVG, and replacing the prior one with this much better version. I am hoping to achieve a seamless, high-quality visual in the hero section.\n\n\n**Finalizing Hero Visual**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the new 3D rotary visual. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and ensuring the animation is smooth across different screen sizes. I\'m also fine-tuning the glow effect and orbital ring motion. My goal is a truly compelling and polished hero section.\n\n\n**Optimizing Visual Performance**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing performance optimization for the hero visual, focusing on keeping it smooth and responsive. I\'m reviewing the implementation, looking for potential bottlenecks. The goal is a captivating, yet performant hero. I\'m excited by the smooth visual experience. I think the users will like the responsive results.\n\n\n**Evaluating User Interaction**\n\nI\'m now assessing how to make the 3D visual interactive, as suggested. I\'m considering adding mouse or touch controls for rotation and exploring incorporating a simple animation on hover. I want to build a captivating, responsive hero experience. I will experiment with the motion library.\n\n\n**Implementing User Interaction**\n\nI\'m now implementing the suggested user interaction features. I\'m focusing on adding mouse controls for rotation and hover animation for a responsive hero experience. I will use the `motion` library to achieve this smoothly and test the results on different screen sizes, hoping to build an intuitive, engaging 3D visual.\n\