    user_intent: "Updating Sponsor Text\n\nThe user wants to change the text \"Official Sponsor of Ring Road Rotaract\" to \"Official Sponsor of Rotaract Club of Ibadan Ring Road\" in the About section of the website."
    session_summary: "The user wants to change the text \"Official Sponsor of Ring Road Rotaract\" to \"Official Sponsor of Rotaract Club of Ibadan Ring Road\" in the About section.\n\nI will edit the `App.tsx` file to reflect this change.\n\n**Summary of Work Done:**\n\n**User\'s Core Objective:**\nThe primary goal was to refine the Rotaract Club website\'s visual presentation, functionality, and branding, with a strong emphasis on ensuring all images and logos displayed correctly, while also enhancing the overall professional polish and user experience.\n\n**Key Features & Modifications:**\n\n1.  **Image Loading Fixes & Enhancements:**\n    *   **Rotary International Logo:**\n        *   Initially struggled with displaying the logo, trying various Wikimedia URLs.\n        *   Switched to a reliable direct PNG link from Wikimedia Commons (`https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e6/Rotary_International_Logo.png`).\n        *   Later, replaced all instances with an embedded **Base64 SVG** for maximum reliability, ensuring it worked even without network access or in restricted environments.\n        *   Finally, updated to an official, high-resolution URL (`https://rotary-ribi.org/upimages/PageMainPics/4_Wheel2013_Transp_1200.png`) for all logo displays.\n        *   Adjusted CSS filters for correct color display (white in Hero, blue in About).\n        *   Removed the redundant Rotary logo from the Hero section\'s text area.\n    *   **Board Member Images:**\n        *   Replaced broken placeholder images with Unsplash URLs, then with reliable, unique URLs from `i.pravatar.cc`.\n        *   Finally, standardized on the **Dicebear API** (`api.dicebear.com/7.x/avataaars/svg`) for all board member avatars, ensuring consistent and high-quality visual representation.\n    *   **Hero Section Visualization:**\n        *   Replaced the initial SVG composition with a dynamic, **3D-rotating gold Rotary wheel** visualization.\n        *   This involved implementing CSS `perspective` and `preserve-3d` for a true 3D effect, with dual-axis rotation (Y-axis spin, X-axis tilt).\n        *   Added visual effects like a pulsating glow, orbital rings, floating \"service particles,\" and a glass-morphism overlay badge.\n\n2.  **Content & Text Updates:**\n    *   **Board of Directors Information:** Replaced placeholder data with authentic names, roles, and detailed bios extracted from the club\'s meeting minutes PDF.\n    *   **District Number:** Updated all mentions of \"District 9125\" to \"District 9126\" across the site (About section, Events description, Footer).\n    *   **Sponsor Text:** Changed the sponsor text in the About section from \"Official Sponsor of Ring Road Rotaract\" to \"Official Sponsor of Rotaract Club of Ibadan Ring Road\".\n\n3.  **Animation & Transition Refinements:**\n    *   **Hero Section Animation:** Changed `whileInView` to `animate` for immediate visibility of text content on load. Removed `viewport={{ once: true }}` for re-animation potential.\n    *   **Board Section Animation:** Adjusted animation properties (`scale`, `delay`, `amount`) for smoother entrance effects on board member cards.\n    *   **General Scroll Animations:** Implemented `viewport={{ once: true, amount: 0.1 }}` for most scroll-triggered elements to ensure they animate smoothly upon entering the viewport.\n    *   **Modal Animations:** Utilized `AnimatePresence` for smooth entry and exit animations of the event details modal.\n\n4.  **Code Structure & Readability:**\n    *   Introduced constants for Base64 logos and official URLs (`ROTARY_LOGO_BASE64`, `ROTARY_LOGO_URL`).\n    *   Organized components and constants logically within `App.tsx`.\n    *   Ensured consistent use of Tailwind CSS classes for styling.\n\n**Dependencies & APIs:**\n*   `@google/genai`: (Not actively used in recent changes, but present in initial setup)\n*   `@tailwindcss/vite`, `autoprefixer`, `tailwindcss`: Core styling utilities.\n*   `@vitejs/plugin-react`, `vite`: Development server and build tools.\n*   `dotenv`: For environment variable management.\n*   `express`: (Likely for local development server setup)\n*   `lucide-react`: Used for various icons throughout the site.\n*   `motion/react`: For advanced animations and scroll-based effects.\n*   `react`, `react-dom`: Core React libraries.\n*   `@types/node`, `@types/express`: TypeScript type definitions.\n*   `tsx`: For running TypeScript directly.\n*   `typescript`: Language transpilation.\n*   **External APIs:**\n    *   `api.dicebear.com`: For generating dynamic user avatars.\n    *   `i.pravatar.cc`: Previously used for avatars.\n    *   `upload.wikimedia.org`, `rotary-ribi.org`: For Rotary logo assets.\n\n**Design Decisions:**\n*   **Professional Polish:** Aimed for a clean, modern, and professional aesthetic, benchmarked against award-winning nonprofit sites.\n*   **Brand Consistency:** Ensured consistent use of Rotaract and Rotary brand colors, fonts, and logos.\n*   **User Experience:** Prioritized smooth animations, clear calls to action, and immediate visibility of key content.\n*   **Reliability:** Implemented strategies (Base64, stable CDNs, Dicebear) to ensure images and logos are always visible.\n*   **Single HTML File Deliverable:** While the current implementation uses React components and Vite, the original goal was a self-contained HTML file. The current structure is production-ready within a React/Vite framework.\n\n**Environmental Variables:**\n*   `.env.example` was present, indicating potential use of `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `APP_URL`, though not directly manipulated in the recent conversation.\n\n**Security Preferences:**\n*   `referrerPolicy=\"no-referrer\"` was consistently applied to external image sources to prevent sending unnecessary referrer information.\n\n**Special User Requests & Preferences:**\n*   Explicit requests to fix image loading issues were a primary driver.\n*   A strong desire for a \"professional polish\" and \"excellent\" visual elements (like the 3D wheel).\n*   Specific instructions for text and data updates (Board info, district number, sponsor text).\n\n**Existing Blockers & Bugs (Resolved):**\n*   **Resolved:** Non-display of Rotary logos and board member images.\n*   **Resolved:** Issues with animation triggers and timing.\n*   **Resolved:** Broken image links.\n\n**Next Steps:**\n*   **Final Visual Review:** Conduct a comprehensive check of all images, logos, and animations across different devices and browsers.\n*   **Content Accuracy:** Ensure all text content is accurate and aligned with the club\'s mission and current information.\n*   **Accessibility Audit:** Verify that alt text is appropriate for all images and that the site meets accessibility standards.\n*   **Performance Optimization:** Consider image optimization (size, format) and lazy loading for further performance gains, especially for the 3D visualization.\n*   **Code Refinement:** Ensure the code is well-commented and adheres to best practices for maintainability.\n\nThis summary provides a detailed overview of all modifications, decisions, and resolved issues, enabling a seamless continuation of development.\n\n<edit_file>{\"Instruction\":\"Change the sponsor text in the About section.\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"                <div className=\\\"text-[10px] font-bold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-[0.2em] leading-tight\\\">\\n                  Official Sponsor of <br /> Rotaract Club of Ibadan Ring Road\\n                </div>\\n\", \"TargetContent\":\"                <div className=\\\"text-[10px] font-bold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-[0.2em] leading-tight\\\">\\n                  Official Sponsor of <br /> Ring Road Rotaract\\n                </div>\\n\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/App.tsx\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating sponsor text in About section.\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update sponsor text\"}</edit_file>"
