    thinking: "**Considering Logo Size**\n\nI\'m focusing on the navbar logo size now. The user thinks it\'s too small. I\'m checking the existing code to see how it\'s implemented.\n\n\n**Analyzing Logo-Navbar Relationship**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into how the logo size relates to the navbar height. It seems I need to consider both the scrolled and un-scrolled states. A larger logo means adjusting the navbar height or padding. I\'m thinking of increasing the logo\'s height to match the navbar height, but I\'m concerned it might feel cramped. I need to consider if the scrolled state should also shrink the logo.\n\n\n**Refining Logo Height Metrics**\n\nI\'m now revisiting the logo\'s height relative to the navbar. My earlier assessments were based on some incorrect assumptions regarding how the `scrolled` state was handled. I\'ve re-examined the code. The existing height ratios didn\'t work. Now I\'m considering `h-20 md:h-24` and `h-16 md:h-18` for the logo in unscrolled/scrolled states. Then I realized I should make sure to re-evaluate how the navbar itself can be sized.\n\n\n**Evaluating Height Increases**\n\nI\'m now determining height increases. I\'m making the logo and navbar dynamic, based on the scrolled state. I\'ve revised the plan based on user feedback. The logo will use `h-24 md:h-32` when unscrolled, and `h-14 md:h-16` when scrolled. The navbar will use `h-32 md:h-40` and `h-20` respectively. But now I need to check the exact logo aspect ratio and what looks best with the image.\n\n\n"
